def average_score(scores):
    total = 0
    for i in range(1, len(scores)):
        total = total + scores[i]
    return total / len(scores)

In plain English, this code says: start the total at 0, go through the list of scores and add each one to the total, then divide the total by how many scores there are. One thing to know: in this language, counting starts at 0, not 1. So the first score is number 0.

The AI said: "This code is correct. It will work for any list of scores." The student tested it one time with the scores 80, 90, and 100. It printed 63.3, and the student wrote it down as the answer.
